  "name": "Southern Udmurt village song (Kiyasovo)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Non-ritual village song of the southern Udmurts, documented in the Kiyasovo district of the Udmurt Republic by the ethnomusicologist Irina Pchelovodova and the folklorist Nikolai Anisimov and published online by the Estonian Literary Museum as Songs of the Southern Udmurt. The repertoire spans lyrical songs, chastushki, dancing and game songs, teasing songs and songs borrowed from neighbours, and is a separate regional repertoire from the improvised krez singing of the northern Udmurts; the Besermyan of north-western Udmurtia keep yet another local tradition not modelled here.",
